From b4f88aa64f7a2d787f88440c20ae810eac59b19b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NEXUS <nexus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:01:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/27] nexus_engine: keep the engine state alive until the
 process ends

After a session the engine thread has finished but is joined only when the
next session starts. At process exit the static Engine was destroyed with a
joinable std::thread, which calls std::terminate: NEXUS.exe ended with
0xC0000409 when it closed after having run a game. The state object is now
never destroyed (the OS reclaims it), like other process-lifetime singletons.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X7yw1ZJY9GYi2KYHfiXxvY
(cherry picked from commit 55e161862042fdd6b94dec3d54721f94254ecceb)
---
 src/nexus_engine/nexus_engine.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nexus_engine/nexus_engine.cpp b/src/nexus_engine/nexus_engine.cpp
index 5bb77ffb2..5b75b5358 100644
--- a/src/nexus_engine/nexus_engine.cpp
+++ b/src/nexus_engine/nexus_engine.cpp
@@ -123,8 +123,11 @@ struct Engine {
 };
 
 Engine& E() {
-    static Engine engine;
-    return engine;
+    // Never destroyed: at process exit Windows has already ended the engine thread, and
+    // destroying a finished-but-unjoined std::thread (or tearing Core::System down inside
+    // DLL_PROCESS_DETACH) would end the host process with a fail-fast error instead of exiting.
+    static Engine* const engine = new Engine;
+    return *engine;
 }
 
 void Fail(const char* code, const std::string& message) {
